[
  {
    "id": "sitl42-tab",
    "type": "tab",
    "label": "SITL 43 Follow leader",
    "disabled": false,
    "info": "Flow-level follow-leader on ArduPilot sysids 1–5: fly the fleet, move leader sysid 1 sixty metres north, and let a 1 Hz position gate re-anchor a wedge of followers (2–5) on the leader's live position (mavlink-formation anchorMode=leader). A State-feed watchdog holds the loop on leader link loss and resumes on heartbeat.",
    "env": []
  },
  {
    "id": "sitl42-comment",
    "type": "comment",
    "z": "sitl42-tab",
    "name": "Follow-leader: move leader, wedge chases",
    "info": "Prerequisite: fleet arm-ready (harness prep ap-arm-ready-fleet).\n\nFlight chain: GUIDED ×5 → arm ×5 → takeoff 30 m ×5 → climb settle → stream GLOBAL_POSITION_INT (33) at 2 Hz on sysid 1 → move the LEADER 60 m north (single-member formation, fixed anchor).\n\nFollow loop (live from deploy): In (leader position, 1 Hz) → minMove gate (15 m horizontal) → Formation anchorMode=leader re-anchors followers 2–5 in a 10 m wedge — one confirmed DO_REPOSITION fan-out per accepted update. The gate seeds its baseline on the first fix WITHOUT firing: re-anchors are movement-driven, never stream-start-driven.\n\nWatchdog: State feed (stale/expired/peer-new/heartbeat) holds the loop while the leader link is stale/expired — followers keep their last commanded positions — and auto-resumes on heartbeat.\n\nVerdict: `leader move status` succeeded (count 1) AND a `reanchor status` aggregate succeeded with count: 4.",
    "x": 320,
    "y": 40,
    "wires": []
  },
